1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,850
This is MEMENTO: an intelligent personal memory and conversation analysis device built for Hack Club's Half Life.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:13,025
Most voice recorders are just digital dustbins: you record hours of audio and never open them again.

3
00:00:13,025 --> 00:00:15,312
MEMENTO changes that.

4
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:26,950
It's a wearable clip-on powered by an ESP32-S3 and an INMP441 digital MEMS microphone that records high-fidelity 16kHz audio straight to local microSD storage.

5
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:35,112
It features a physical hardware mute switch that cuts power to the mic capsule, a silent haptic feedback motor, and a glanceable OLED display.

6
00:00:35,112 --> 00:00:40,137
When you plug it into your Mac, everything is processed 100% offline.

7
00:00:40,137 --> 00:00:47,500
Local Whisper handles transcription, PyAnnote separates speakers, and Librosa analyzes vocal tone and hesitation.

8
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:56,250
Then our local AI acts as your interview coach: highlighting where you dodged questions, tracking promises made, and compiling a daily executive summary.

9
00:00:56,250 --> 00:01:01,112
Designed from scratch, fully open source, and built for under 60 dollars.

